<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="container">
    <span class="eyebrow eyebrow--center">About</span>
    <h1 class="page-hero__title">Document tools that respect your privacy</h1>
    <p class="page-hero__lead">
      <%= site.name %> brings the everyday document tools people actually need into one clean,
      browser-based workspace — built so your files stay on your device.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container prose">
    <h2>What <%= site.name %> is</h2>
    <p>
      <%= site.name %> is a free, browser-based platform for working with PDFs and documents. Instead
      of installing heavy software or uploading sensitive files to a cloud service, you open your
      document in the browser and get straight to work. Merging, splitting, editing, converting,
      signing, writing and charting all happen in one place.
    </p>

    <h2>The problem we set out to solve</h2>
    <p>
      Simple document tasks are often far harder than they should be. You end up hunting for a
      website to merge two PDFs, another to compress a file, and yet another to convert it — usually
      uploading your document to a stranger’s server each time. <%= site.name %> pulls these everyday
      jobs together into a single, well-designed workspace, and keeps the processing on your own
      device so you don’t have to trade privacy for convenience.
    </p>

    <h2>What you can do</h2>
    <div class="value-grid value-grid--about">
      <div class="value">
        <h3>PDF tools</h3>
        <p>Merge, split, compress, organize, edit and sign PDFs — reorder pages, add text and images, and export a finished file.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="value">
        <h3>Document editor</h3>
        <p>A clean, Google Docs-style editor for writing letters, reports and notes with headings, tables, images, headers and footers.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="value">
        <h3>Charts &amp; graphs</h3>
        <p>Turn your data into editable bar, line and pie charts and drop them straight into a document.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="value">
        <h3>Convert &amp; export</h3>
        <p>Move between PDF, Word, HTML and image formats, and export tables to Excel (.xlsx) for further analysis.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="value">
        <h3>Spreadsheets (in development)</h3>
        <p>Today you can convert and export to Excel. A dedicated in-browser spreadsheet editor is on our roadmap.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="value">
        <h3>AI tools (preview)</h3>
        <p>Where AI-assisted features are offered, they are designed to run on-device — no cloud AI provider, no API keys, no uploads.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>Who it’s for</h2>
    <p>
      <%= site.name %> is built for anyone who works with documents but doesn’t want the overhead of
      desktop office suites: students assembling assignments, freelancers signing contracts, small
      businesses producing reports and proposals, and everyday users who just need to fix a PDF
      quickly. If your task is a normal document job, we want it to take seconds.
    </p>

    <h2>Our focus: simple document workflows</h2>
    <p>
      We deliberately concentrate on the common jobs people do again and again, and try to make each
      one obvious and fast. Rather than piling on rarely-used features, we invest in clarity — sensible
      defaults, a calm interface, and tools that behave the way you expect. As the platform grows, new
      capabilities are added carefully so the experience stays simple.
    </p>

    <h2>Our approach to privacy and security</h2>
    <p>
      Privacy isn’t a bolt-on for us; it shapes how the product is built. Your files are processed in
      your browser and are not uploaded to our servers. There is no account required and no document
      database on our side to be exposed. You can read the specifics on our
      <a href="/security">Security page</a> and in our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <div class="about-cta">
      <a href="/workspace" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">Open the editor</a>
      <a href="/tools" class="btn btn-outline btn-lg">Explore the tools</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
